|name2 = Lunos the Luminous
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Lunos the Luminous''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Squire Luno's primary value comes from his [[Conjure]], acting as a pocket [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] that can be activated once every time the unit is sent out. With how cheap and spammable this cat is, he absolutely breaks difficulty in half being capable of repeatedly [[Knockback|Knocking back]] all enemies consistently every time he recharges. This applies to most stages in the game, to the point where any stage you can think of right now is probably obliterated by him. Squire Luno himself is a decent tanker against his target traits, but dies very quickly with how reliant he is on his [[Resistant|Resistance]] to Dark/Angel/Aku/Relic; his performance is usually overshadowed by the sheer utility of his Conjure.

The stats and Conjure in his Normal Form are directly inferior to his Evolved Form's. However, Squire Luno is much cheaper and more thus suited for as a generalist Conjurer or in cash-tight stages. Moving to the front faster and dying faster also means more Conjured spirits to summon, despite the spirits having less range and Mini-Surge level. The only real weakness with Squire Luno is against enemies who are Immune to Knockback or Surge, since he provides almost nothing outside of that crowd-control. Additionally, it can be dangerous to use him against rebound enemies, where the location of his Mini-Surge is entirely random and can end up backfiring if you fail to anticipate how the enemy interacts with it.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Lunos the Luminous is completely ridiculous in every regard. He possesses an identical recharge rate to his Normal Form, with an even more powerful Conjure that deals 91,800 damage at Lv.30 (145,800 at Lv.50) per cast, accounting for the level 5 [[Surge Attack#Mini-Surge|Mini-Surge]]. The Knockback ability in said Conjure finds immense utility in a similar manner to [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]]'s Knockback, except against all traits and at an even higher Surge level than Doron.

He can easily prevent enemies with long attack animations from ever attacking, and can keep bosses locked in place at the Enemy Base without protest while he quickly beats them to a bloody pulp regardless of their typing. In the event that he dies, you can simply cycle him out again to continue where you left off immediately thanks to his 10-second recharge. He is marginally expensive, so you do need to watch the wallet to ensure you're not draining cash too quickly with each death. Even then, him dying can be seen as advantageous in many situations too, since that just means another Conjure directly to the enemy's face. Lunos is immune to most negative status effects, and cannot be forced to reposition through any means other than Warp or a damage knockback. Along with his high bulk, this means that he will always be fully capable of approaching his target unhindered, always getting him in place for a high value Conjure. However, just like his Normal Form, enemies who are Immune to Knockback and Surge are not very good targets to use Lunos the Luminous against. He generally fares better than Squire Luno in these situations, given his stat advantage, so consider using this form if you absolutely must.

To say he is amazing would be a gross understatement, as Lunos the Luminous is unbelievably broken all around, even comparatively to ordinary [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] standards.

