==Trivia==
*Squire Luno was first made obtainable in [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]] on January 1st, 2026.
**In [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]], he was first made obtainable on February 13th, 2026.
*Squire Luno is a counterpart to [[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Celestial Child Luna]]:
**The names Luno and Luna are only one letter apart. In some languages, the last letter determines the character's gender. In this case, '''o''' is for male and '''a''' is for female.
**Luno and Luna have the same moon symbols across their forms.
**Their Japanese descriptions both say that they do not know their own mission.
**Both have Omni Strike, immunity to Curse and [[Special Abilities|abilities]] that target four traits, including [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]], while having an EPICFEST counterpart that targets four other traits.
*Squire Luno's [[Conjure|Conjured]] spirit is the only one to deviate from the standard 45,900 attack power at level 30.
**Additionally, it has a uniquely shorter range than all other spirits, and along with [[Mamoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Mamolan Pasalan]], they are the only spirits to not have 800 range.
*Although one of Lunos the Luminous's eyes is covered, sprites for both exist in his spritesheet.
*A squire is a term in medieval times practically meaning a knight's attendant or apprentice.

